G'day all. I'm pleased to announce hledger 2.0 preview release 3.
Highlights:

- conventional file layout for rules/data/prices
- get command
- commodity aliases
- print aligns by decimal mark
- more intuitive precision behaviour
- more robust lot detection
- average cost basis methods
- customisable report titles
- prices --summary report
- a more robust roi report.

Release notes, install docs, user manual:

- https://hledger.org/relnotes.html#2026-06-24-hledger-1993
- https://hledger.org/install
- https://hledger.org/dev/hledger.html

Release contributors:

Simon Michael,
Dmitry Astapov,
Henning Thielemann,
Adam Sardo,
Rostislav Raykov.


hledger is accounting software, for both beginners and experts,
that uses human-readable, version-controllable, future-proof plain text files.
It's free, fast, friendly, dependable, GPL-licensed, cross-platform,
double-entry, multi-currency, multi-interface, and fun to use.

It can help you learn bookkeeping.. untangle accounting messes..
track your financial status and history.. run forecasts..
set budgets and saving goals.. produce detailed time reports..
convert/transform financial data.. validate other systems..
and create more balance and calm in your life.

For more info, see https://hledger.org. (And if it's providing value to
you, consider becoming a https://hledger.org/sponsor.html !)


